KORTEX PAST EXAMINATION PAPERS
CS - Algorithms & Data Structures (Year 2024)

Q1. What is the worst-case runtime complexity of QuickSort on an already sorted array using first-element pivot?
  (A) O(N log N)
  (B) O(N)
  (C) O(N^2)
  (D) O(log N)
  Answer: C - Picking first element as pivot on a sorted list yields unbalanced partitions of size (N-1) and 0, resulting in O(N^2).


